Consider $abs(vb(x) - lambda vb(y))^2 >= 0$ for $lambda in RR$. Expanding,
$ abs(vb(x))^2 + lambda^2 abs(vb(y))^2 - 2 lambda vb(x) dot vb(y) >= 0 $
is a quadratic in $lambda$ that never becomes negative, so its discriminant is non-positive:
$ 4 (vb(x) dot vb(y))^2 - 4 abs(vb(x))^2 abs(vb(y))^2 <= 0. $
Rearranging gives $abs(vb(x) dot vb(y)) <= abs(vb(x)) abs(vb(y))$.
